{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917446255},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a calculation: farmers markets per 100,000 residents in the U.S. They've provided two data sources and want the answer to four decimal places with no unverified facts.\n\nI need to:\n1. Orient first by checking if there are semantic models and existing aliases in the catalog\n2. Get the total farmers markets from the first CSV\n3. Get the total U.S. residents from the census CSV\n4. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n5. Use xorq_select to get these values and xorq_verify to verify them\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog for semantic models and existing aliases.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents using the xorq catalog. Let me start by checking what's available in the catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01TUpJscqtwBfKpdnz9HVeXv","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Mf9KLjdMkuLCdB7LC729FX","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":300,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8306,"totalTokens":8616,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0015,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.0103825,"total":0.0118925},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reaso